<title>USA: CCC seeks 7,220 tonnes U.S. HRW wheat for Bosnia.</title>
<headline>CCC seeks 7,220 tonnes U.S. HRW wheat for Bosnia.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commodity Credit Corp said it was seeking up to 7,220 tonnes of U.S. No. 2 or better hard red winter wheat, maximum moisture 13.5 percent, under the export program for Bosnia.</p>
<p>The shipment period was set for May 7-31.</p>
<p>Offers are due April 21.</p>
<p>CCC, which is part of USDA, said the wheat must originate in areas of the United States where Tilletia Indica (Karnal Bunt) is not known to occur.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
